[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [[:db/retract 17592186220900 :answer-field/choices 17592186220904] [:db/retract 17592186220900 :answer-field/choices 17592186220901] [:db/retract 17592186220900 :answer-field/choices 17592186220902] [:db/retract 17592186220900 :answer-field/choices 17592186220903] {:db/id 17592186221457 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-f846bdbb-b4eb-53cc-9341-26d00f9d6239"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186221455 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-8a503430-335a-52ca-a8f2-1a25c8b18de5" "question-336eb7d8-27df-584e-adc9-df5d1de8bc4e"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-8a503430-335a-52ca-a8f2-1a25c8b18de5" :question/id #uuid "8a503430-335a-52ca-a8f2-1a25c8b18de5" :question/math-academy-id "q-343819" :question/problem "Select the missing parts in a particular solution of the differential equation ${y}^{′}+3y=f(x),$ where the Fourier series of the $4$-periodic forcing function is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{2(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi }sin\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}).\n$$\n\nThe Fourier series of a particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,{{field-1}}\\cdot cos\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})+{{field-2}}\\cdot sin\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We assume that a solution of our equation has the following Fourier series:\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}cos\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})+{b}_{n}sin\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}).\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p}^{′} & ∼\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}cos\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})+{b}_{n}sin\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})) \\\\  & ∼0+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\cdot (-\\frac{n\\pi }{2}sin\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}))+{b}_{n}\\cdot \\frac{n\\pi }{2}cos\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}) \\\\  & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-\\frac{{a}_{n}n\\pi }{2}sin\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})+\\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{2}cos\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the expressions for ${y}_{p}^{′}$ and ${y}_{p}$ into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ({\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-\\frac{{a}_{n}n\\pi }{2}sin\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})+\\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{2}cos\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})) \\\\  & \\,+3(\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}cos\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})+{b}_{n}sin\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})) \\\\  & \\,\\,={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{2(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi }sin\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRearranging the terms, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\frac{3{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }(\\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{2}+3{a}_{n})cos\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}) \\\\  & \\,\\,+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }(-\\frac{{a}_{n}n\\pi }{2}+3{b}_{n})sin\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}) \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{2(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi }sin\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, equating the free terms and the cosine and sine coefficients, we obtain the following system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3{a}_{0}}{2}=0 \\\\ \\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{2}+3{a}_{n}=0 \\\\ -\\frac{{a}_{n}n\\pi }{2}+3{b}_{n}=\\frac{2(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, ${a}_{0}=0.$ \n\nNext, from the second equation, \n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=-\\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{6}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the third equation gives\n\n$$\n-(-\\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{6})\\frac{n\\pi }{2}+3{b}_{n}=\\frac{2(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi }\\,⇒\\,{b}_{n}=\\frac{24(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+36)}\n$$\n\nTherefore, for ${a}_{n}$ with $n\\ge 1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =-\\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{6} \\\\  & =-\\frac{n\\pi }{6}\\cdot \\frac{24(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+36)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+36}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,-\\frac{4(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+36}\\cdot cos\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})+\\frac{24(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+36)}\\cdot sin\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-819e15d7-2e20-52a4-83ba-4e170679fa89" "answer-field-34398e9c-a70c-53b7-b84a-4a5e338eee91"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-819e15d7-2e20-52a4-83ba-4e170679fa89" :answer-field/id #uuid "819e15d7-2e20-52a4-83ba-4e170679fa89" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-ab325d87-a065-546e-baf7-139015307fa0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-30256479-a0c3-536f-992c-58c727330693" "answer-ab325d87-a065-546e-baf7-139015307fa0" "answer-644342fd-f897-5f58-92a1-0b8ef53eb76b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-30256479-a0c3-536f-992c-58c727330693" :answer/id #uuid "30256479-a0c3-536f-992c-58c727330693" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{12(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+36)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ab325d87-a065-546e-baf7-139015307fa0" :answer/id #uuid "ab325d87-a065-546e-baf7-139015307fa0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{4(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+36}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-644342fd-f897-5f58-92a1-0b8ef53eb76b" :answer/id #uuid "644342fd-f897-5f58-92a1-0b8ef53eb76b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{(-1)^{n}}{n({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+36)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-34398e9c-a70c-53b7-b84a-4a5e338eee91" :answer-field/id #uuid "34398e9c-a70c-53b7-b84a-4a5e338eee91" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-85bccb7d-0294-553d-b094-d5837f950d47" :answer-field/choices ["answer-78061c99-9116-56c2-88f4-777413d48782" "answer-f77c27c9-c7d3-591e-bac3-638faae40001" "answer-85bccb7d-0294-553d-b094-d5837f950d47"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-78061c99-9116-56c2-88f4-777413d48782" :answer/id #uuid "78061c99-9116-56c2-88f4-777413d48782" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{18(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+36)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f77c27c9-c7d3-591e-bac3-638faae40001" :answer/id #uuid "f77c27c9-c7d3-591e-bac3-638faae40001" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{12(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+36)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-85bccb7d-0294-553d-b094-d5837f950d47" :answer/id #uuid "85bccb7d-0294-553d-b094-d5837f950d47" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{24(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+36)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-336eb7d8-27df-584e-adc9-df5d1de8bc4e" :question/id #uuid "336eb7d8-27df-584e-adc9-df5d1de8bc4e" :question/math-academy-id "q-344058" :question/problem "Select the missing parts in a particular solution of the differential equation ${y}^{′}-3y=f(x),$ where the Fourier series of the $6$-periodic forcing function is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼-3+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{6}{{n}^{2}\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}).\n$$\n\nThe Fourier series of a particular solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p}∼{{field-1}} & +{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,{{field-2}}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}) \\\\  & +{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,{{field-3}}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We assume that a solution of our equation has the following Fourier series:\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}).\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p}^{′} & ∼\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})) \\\\  & ∼0+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\cdot (-\\frac{n\\pi }{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}))+{b}_{n}\\cdot \\frac{n\\pi }{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}) \\\\  & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-\\frac{{a}_{n}n\\pi }{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})+\\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the expressions for ${y}_{p}^{′}$ and ${y}_{p}$ into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ({\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-\\frac{{a}_{n}n\\pi }{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})+\\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})) \\\\  & \\,-3(\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})) \\\\  & \\,\\,=-3+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{6}{{n}^{2}\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRearranging the terms, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & -3\\cdot \\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }(\\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{3}-3{a}_{n})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}) \\\\  & \\,\\,+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }(-\\frac{{a}_{n}n\\pi }{3}-3{b}_{n})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}) \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,=-3+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{6}{{n}^{2}\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, equating the free terms and the coefficients next to sines and cosines, we obtain the following system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-3\\cdot \\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}=-3 \\\\ \\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{3}-3{a}_{n}=\\frac{6}{{n}^{2}\\pi } \\\\ -\\frac{{a}_{n}n\\pi }{3}-3{b}_{n}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, ${a}_{0}=2,$ which means the constant term is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}=1.\n$$\n\nNext, from the third equation, \n\n$$\n{b}_{n}=-\\frac{{a}_{n}n\\pi }{9}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation gives\n\n$$\n(-\\frac{{a}_{n}n\\pi }{9})\\frac{n\\pi }{3}-3{a}_{n}=\\frac{6}{{n}^{2}\\pi }\\,⇒\\,{a}_{n}=-\\frac{162}{{n}^{2}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+81)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, for ${a}_{n}$ with $n\\ge 1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{n} & =-\\frac{{a}_{n}n\\pi }{9} \\\\  & =-\\frac{n\\pi }{9}\\cdot (-\\frac{162}{{n}^{2}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+81)}) \\\\  & =\\frac{18}{n({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+81)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p}∼1 & +{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,-\\frac{162}{{n}^{2}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+81)}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}) \\\\  & +{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,\\frac{18}{n({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+81)}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-319f9cc5-6350-50bc-9ef5-9fc966e9afe8" "answer-field-cdd62ed7-f5a0-5d14-b295-af477d1b5a66" "answer-field-44914850-8fa0-5396-b873-81fa2f52fbd0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-319f9cc5-6350-50bc-9ef5-9fc966e9afe8" :answer-field/id #uuid "319f9cc5-6350-50bc-9ef5-9fc966e9afe8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-efdbe697-d6a3-508c-a692-ae48f85ba690" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b7737c7e-9824-5e5f-a3ae-34856a098e7c" "answer-ab11db4e-65b6-5238-aa40-285ffcaa4e1d" "answer-efdbe697-d6a3-508c-a692-ae48f85ba690" "answer-55053340-f635-546e-8e5d-4621e256edb8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b7737c7e-9824-5e5f-a3ae-34856a098e7c" :answer/id #uuid "b7737c7e-9824-5e5f-a3ae-34856a098e7c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ab11db4e-65b6-5238-aa40-285ffcaa4e1d" :answer/id #uuid "ab11db4e-65b6-5238-aa40-285ffcaa4e1d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-efdbe697-d6a3-508c-a692-ae48f85ba690" :answer/id #uuid "efdbe697-d6a3-508c-a692-ae48f85ba690" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-55053340-f635-546e-8e5d-4621e256edb8" :answer/id #uuid "55053340-f635-546e-8e5d-4621e256edb8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-cdd62ed7-f5a0-5d14-b295-af477d1b5a66" :answer-field/id #uuid "cdd62ed7-f5a0-5d14-b295-af477d1b5a66" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-92481f36-1e85-521a-ba9a-acee004b176f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-92481f36-1e85-521a-ba9a-acee004b176f" "answer-46ca47af-c6a7-509f-8d83-2150c0238a78" "answer-e0c34785-8282-5217-a833-be2afab68c64"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-92481f36-1e85-521a-ba9a-acee004b176f" :answer/id #uuid "92481f36-1e85-521a-ba9a-acee004b176f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{162}{{n}^{2}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+81)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-46ca47af-c6a7-509f-8d83-2150c0238a78" :answer/id #uuid "46ca47af-c6a7-509f-8d83-2150c0238a78" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{18}{{n}^{2}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+81)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e0c34785-8282-5217-a833-be2afab68c64" :answer/id #uuid "e0c34785-8282-5217-a833-be2afab68c64" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{162}{{n}^{2}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+81)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-44914850-8fa0-5396-b873-81fa2f52fbd0" :answer-field/id #uuid "44914850-8fa0-5396-b873-81fa2f52fbd0" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-e29b2edf-998e-5740-bb95-54727e9f45f8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e29b2edf-998e-5740-bb95-54727e9f45f8" "answer-1b3542e3-4bf3-5d25-87cb-feba5f3ffd90" "answer-5558f4a3-3994-5897-8ff9-622d5df04392"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e29b2edf-998e-5740-bb95-54727e9f45f8" :answer/id #uuid "e29b2edf-998e-5740-bb95-54727e9f45f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{18}{n({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+81)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1b3542e3-4bf3-5d25-87cb-feba5f3ffd90" :answer/id #uuid "1b3542e3-4bf3-5d25-87cb-feba5f3ffd90" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{18}{{n}^{2}({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+81)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5558f4a3-3994-5897-8ff9-622d5df04392" :answer/id #uuid "5558f4a3-3994-5897-8ff9-622d5df04392" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{6}{n({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+81)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186222035 :question/problem "Select the missing parts in a particular solution of the differential equation ${y}^{″}-9y=f(x),$ where the Fourier series of the $2$-periodic forcing function is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{\\pi }{{n}^{3}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x).\n$$\n\n*Hint: You may assume that the free term and all the sine coefficients in the Fourier series of the particular solution are equal to zero.*\n\nThe Fourier series of a particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,{{field-1}}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x)\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We assume that a solution of our equation has the following Fourier series:\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x).\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p}^{′} & ∼\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x))∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-{a}_{n}n\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi x) \\\\ {y}_{p}^{″} & ∼\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-{a}_{n}n\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi x))∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-{a}_{n}{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the expressions for ${y}_{p}^{″}$ and ${y}_{p}$ into the equation and have\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-{a}_{n}{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x)-9({\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x))={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{\\pi }{{n}^{3}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x).\n$$\n\nRearranging the terms, we get \n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-{a}_{n}({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+9)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x)={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{\\pi }{{n}^{3}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x).\n$$\n\nNow, equating the cosine coefficients, we obtain \n\n$$\n-{a}_{n}({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+9)=\\frac{\\pi }{{n}^{3}}\\,⇒\\,{a}_{n}=-\\frac{\\pi }{{n}^{3}({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+9)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,-\\frac{\\pi }{{n}^{3}({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+9)}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186220900 :answer-field/correct "answer-569abf23-828d-556a-8f5f-a80cd2b16ce5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ec30d690-d89c-5e99-97e6-bdae59c5d3d2" "answer-569abf23-828d-556a-8f5f-a80cd2b16ce5" "answer-ff05bb1d-0d47-5a0b-9d42-84f03013e335" "answer-a4c02cbf-419a-5b32-acdf-ac8babf2fa7a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ec30d690-d89c-5e99-97e6-bdae59c5d3d2" :answer/id #uuid "ec30d690-d89c-5e99-97e6-bdae59c5d3d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{n({n}^{3}\\pi -9)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-569abf23-828d-556a-8f5f-a80cd2b16ce5" :answer/id #uuid "569abf23-828d-556a-8f5f-a80cd2b16ce5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{{n}^{3}({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+9)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ff05bb1d-0d47-5a0b-9d42-84f03013e335" :answer/id #uuid "ff05bb1d-0d47-5a0b-9d42-84f03013e335" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{n}^{3}{\\pi }^{2}({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}-9)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a4c02cbf-419a-5b32-acdf-ac8babf2fa7a" :answer/id #uuid "a4c02cbf-419a-5b32-acdf-ac8babf2fa7a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{n+1}{{n}^{3}{\\pi }^{2}+9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-f846bdbb-b4eb-53cc-9341-26d00f9d6239" :question/id #uuid "f846bdbb-b4eb-53cc-9341-26d00f9d6239" :question/math-academy-id "q-343906" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation ${y}^{″}+{\\pi }^{2}y=f(x),$ where the $2$-periodic forcing function is given by \n\n$$\nf(x)∼4+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{9}{{n}^{2}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi x).\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below regarding the resonant component of a particular solution of the equation.\n\nThe natural frequency of the system matches the frequency of the {{field-1}} harmonic of the forcing function. \n\nConsequently, the particular solution contains a resonant term of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{{p}_{1}}={{field-2}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We begin by identifying resonance. The differential equation \n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+{\\pi }^{2}y=f(x)\n$$\n\nhas a natural frequency of \n\n$$\n\\omega =\\sqrt{{\\pi }^{2}}=\\pi .\n$$\n\nThe frequencies of the forcing harmonics for a $2$-periodic function $(L=1)$ are \n\n$$\n{\\omega }_{n}=\\frac{n\\pi }{1}=n\\pi .\n$$\n\nFor $n=1$, we have ${\\omega }_{1}=\\pi .$ Since ${\\omega }_{1}=\\omega ,$ the $n=1$ harmonic of the forcing function causes resonance.\n\nFor the $n=1$ harmonic, the forcing term is \n\n$$\n{f}_{1}(x)=9\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x).\n$$\n\nBecause this frequency matches the natural frequency, we assume a particular solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{{p}_{1}}=x(A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)).\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{{p}_{1}}^{′} & =(A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x))+x(-\\pi A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)+\\pi B\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)) \\\\ {y}_{{p}_{1}}^{″} & =-2\\pi A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)+2\\pi B\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)-{\\pi }^{2}x(A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the expressions for ${y}_{{p}_{1}}^{″}$ and ${y}_{{p}_{1}}$ into the equation ${y}^{″}+{\\pi }^{2}y=9\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x):$\n\n$$\n[-2\\pi A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)+2\\pi B\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)-{\\pi }^{2}{y}_{{p}_{1}}]+{\\pi }^{2}{y}_{{p}_{1}}=9\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)\n$$\n\nThe resonant terms involving $x$ cancel out, leaving\n\n$$\n-2\\pi A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)+2\\pi B\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)=9\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x).\n$$\n\nNow, equating the sine and cosine coefficients, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-2\\pi A=9 \\\\ 2\\pi B=0\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}A=-\\frac{9}{2\\pi } \\\\ B=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the resonant component of a particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{{p}_{1}}=-\\frac{9x}{2\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8ce88b2e-b185-5d2e-8cfe-5be89cc0aa87" "answer-field-1e995e02-d0ce-5ccb-a037-04ceee50e084"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8ce88b2e-b185-5d2e-8cfe-5be89cc0aa87" :answer-field/id #uuid "8ce88b2e-b185-5d2e-8cfe-5be89cc0aa87" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-ccea3e9e-29c1-513f-99b9-7b21823c4113" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ccea3e9e-29c1-513f-99b9-7b21823c4113" "answer-27429d6e-d26b-57af-88d8-b3b645dceff5" "answer-83ac4344-49cc-52a5-af95-e3d90acd43a2" "answer-5774f527-99ad-5f17-a48d-89c6006f3a3d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ccea3e9e-29c1-513f-99b9-7b21823c4113" :answer/id #uuid "ccea3e9e-29c1-513f-99b9-7b21823c4113" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "n=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-27429d6e-d26b-57af-88d8-b3b645dceff5" :answer/id #uuid "27429d6e-d26b-57af-88d8-b3b645dceff5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "n=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-83ac4344-49cc-52a5-af95-e3d90acd43a2" :answer/id #uuid "83ac4344-49cc-52a5-af95-e3d90acd43a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "n=3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5774f527-99ad-5f17-a48d-89c6006f3a3d" :answer/id #uuid "5774f527-99ad-5f17-a48d-89c6006f3a3d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "n=4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1e995e02-d0ce-5ccb-a037-04ceee50e084" :answer-field/id #uuid "1e995e02-d0ce-5ccb-a037-04ceee50e084" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-a4ade4ea-e129-57c8-abf7-ee1ae4a37fe1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a4ade4ea-e129-57c8-abf7-ee1ae4a37fe1" "answer-65f57259-781b-593f-95c6-d5d30ac088ef" "answer-a913ed3d-a5ff-575d-afb5-86ec312e2921" "answer-23e85abf-8716-50e3-935c-317dbb984f0b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a4ade4ea-e129-57c8-abf7-ee1ae4a37fe1" :answer/id #uuid "a4ade4ea-e129-57c8-abf7-ee1ae4a37fe1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{9x}{2\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-65f57259-781b-593f-95c6-d5d30ac088ef" :answer/id #uuid "65f57259-781b-593f-95c6-d5d30ac088ef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{9x}{4\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a913ed3d-a5ff-575d-afb5-86ec312e2921" :answer/id #uuid "a913ed3d-a5ff-575d-afb5-86ec312e2921" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{9x}{8\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-23e85abf-8716-50e3-935c-317dbb984f0b" :answer/id #uuid "23e85abf-8716-50e3-935c-317dbb984f0b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9x}{4\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]}] "assertions" [["question-8a503430-335a-52ca-a8f2-1a25c8b18de5" :question/id #uuid "8a503430-335a-52ca-a8f2-1a25c8b18de5"] ["question-8a503430-335a-52ca-a8f2-1a25c8b18de5" :question/math-academy-id "q-343819"] ["question-8a503430-335a-52ca-a8f2-1a25c8b18de5" :question/problem "Select the missing parts in a particular solution of the differential equation ${y}^{′}+3y=f(x),$ where the Fourier series of the $4$-periodic forcing function is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{2(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi }sin\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}).\n$$\n\nThe Fourier series of a particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,{{field-1}}\\cdot cos\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})+{{field-2}}\\cdot sin\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})\n$$"] ["question-8a503430-335a-52ca-a8f2-1a25c8b18de5" :question/worked-solution "We assume that a solution of our equation has the following Fourier series:\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}cos\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})+{b}_{n}sin\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}).\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p}^{′} & ∼\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}cos\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})+{b}_{n}sin\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})) \\\\  & ∼0+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\cdot (-\\frac{n\\pi }{2}sin\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}))+{b}_{n}\\cdot \\frac{n\\pi }{2}cos\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}) \\\\  & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-\\frac{{a}_{n}n\\pi }{2}sin\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})+\\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{2}cos\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the expressions for ${y}_{p}^{′}$ and ${y}_{p}$ into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ({\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-\\frac{{a}_{n}n\\pi }{2}sin\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})+\\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{2}cos\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})) \\\\  & \\,+3(\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}cos\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})+{b}_{n}sin\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})) \\\\  & \\,\\,={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{2(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi }sin\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRearranging the terms, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\frac{3{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }(\\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{2}+3{a}_{n})cos\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}) \\\\  & \\,\\,+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }(-\\frac{{a}_{n}n\\pi }{2}+3{b}_{n})sin\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}) \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{2(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi }sin\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, equating the free terms and the cosine and sine coefficients, we obtain the following system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3{a}_{0}}{2}=0 \\\\ \\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{2}+3{a}_{n}=0 \\\\ -\\frac{{a}_{n}n\\pi }{2}+3{b}_{n}=\\frac{2(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, ${a}_{0}=0.$ \n\nNext, from the second equation, \n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=-\\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{6}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the third equation gives\n\n$$\n-(-\\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{6})\\frac{n\\pi }{2}+3{b}_{n}=\\frac{2(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi }\\,⇒\\,{b}_{n}=\\frac{24(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+36)}\n$$\n\nTherefore, for ${a}_{n}$ with $n\\ge 1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =-\\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{6} \\\\  & =-\\frac{n\\pi }{6}\\cdot \\frac{24(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+36)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+36}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,-\\frac{4(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+36}\\cdot cos\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})+\\frac{24(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+36)}\\cdot sin\\,(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}).\n$$"] ["question-8a503430-335a-52ca-a8f2-1a25c8b18de5" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-819e15d7-2e20-52a4-83ba-4e170679fa89" :answer-field/id #uuid "819e15d7-2e20-52a4-83ba-4e170679fa89"] ["answer-30256479-a0c3-536f-992c-58c727330693" :answer/id #uuid "30256479-a0c3-536f-992c-58c727330693"] ["answer-30256479-a0c3-536f-992c-58c727330693" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-30256479-a0c3-536f-992c-58c727330693" :answer/value "-\\frac{12(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+36)}"] ["answer-ab325d87-a065-546e-baf7-139015307fa0" :answer/id #uuid "ab325d87-a065-546e-baf7-139015307fa0"] ["answer-ab325d87-a065-546e-baf7-139015307fa0" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-ab325d87-a065-546e-baf7-139015307fa0" :answer/value "-\\frac{4(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+36}"] ["answer-644342fd-f897-5f58-92a1-0b8ef53eb76b" :answer/id #uuid "644342fd-f897-5f58-92a1-0b8ef53eb76b"] ["answer-644342fd-f897-5f58-92a1-0b8ef53eb76b" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-644342fd-f897-5f58-92a1-0b8ef53eb76b" :answer/value "\\frac{(-1)^{n}}{n({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+36)}"] ["answer-field-819e15d7-2e20-52a4-83ba-4e170679fa89" :answer-field/key "field-1"] ["answer-field-819e15d7-2e20-52a4-83ba-4e170679fa89" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select] ["answer-field-819e15d7-2e20-52a4-83ba-4e170679fa89" :answer-field/correct "answer-ab325d87-a065-546e-baf7-139015307fa0"] ["answer-field-819e15d7-2e20-52a4-83ba-4e170679fa89" :answer-field/choices "answer-30256479-a0c3-536f-992c-58c727330693"] ["answer-field-819e15d7-2e20-52a4-83ba-4e170679fa89" :answer-field/choices "answer-ab325d87-a065-546e-baf7-139015307fa0"] ["answer-field-819e15d7-2e20-52a4-83ba-4e170679fa89" :answer-field/choices "answer-644342fd-f897-5f58-92a1-0b8ef53eb76b"] ["answer-field-34398e9c-a70c-53b7-b84a-4a5e338eee91" :answer-field/id #uuid "34398e9c-a70c-53b7-b84a-4a5e338eee91"] ["answer-78061c99-9116-56c2-88f4-777413d48782" :answer/id #uuid "78061c99-9116-56c2-88f4-777413d48782"] ["answer-78061c99-9116-56c2-88f4-777413d48782" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-78061c99-9116-56c2-88f4-777413d48782" :answer/value "-\\frac{18(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+36)}"] ["answer-f77c27c9-c7d3-591e-bac3-638faae40001" :answer/id #uuid "f77c27c9-c7d3-591e-bac3-638faae40001"] ["answer-f77c27c9-c7d3-591e-bac3-638faae40001" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-f77c27c9-c7d3-591e-bac3-638faae40001" :answer/value "\\frac{12(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+36)}"] ["answer-85bccb7d-0294-553d-b094-d5837f950d47" :answer/id #uuid "85bccb7d-0294-553d-b094-d5837f950d47"] ["answer-85bccb7d-0294-553d-b094-d5837f950d47" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-85bccb7d-0294-553d-b094-d5837f950d47" :answer/value "\\frac{24(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+36)}"] ["answer-field-34398e9c-a70c-53b7-b84a-4a5e338eee91" :answer-field/key "field-2"] ["answer-field-34398e9c-a70c-53b7-b84a-4a5e338eee91" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select] ["answer-field-34398e9c-a70c-53b7-b84a-4a5e338eee91" :answer-field/correct "answer-85bccb7d-0294-553d-b094-d5837f950d47"] ["answer-field-34398e9c-a70c-53b7-b84a-4a5e338eee91" :answer-field/choices "answer-78061c99-9116-56c2-88f4-777413d48782"] ["answer-field-34398e9c-a70c-53b7-b84a-4a5e338eee91" :answer-field/choices "answer-f77c27c9-c7d3-591e-bac3-638faae40001"] ["answer-field-34398e9c-a70c-53b7-b84a-4a5e338eee91" :answer-field/choices "answer-85bccb7d-0294-553d-b094-d5837f950d47"] ["question-8a503430-335a-52ca-a8f2-1a25c8b18de5" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-819e15d7-2e20-52a4-83ba-4e170679fa89"] ["question-8a503430-335a-52ca-a8f2-1a25c8b18de5" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-34398e9c-a70c-53b7-b84a-4a5e338eee91"] [17592186221455 :knowledge-point/questions "question-8a503430-335a-52ca-a8f2-1a25c8b18de5"] ["question-336eb7d8-27df-584e-adc9-df5d1de8bc4e" :question/id #uuid "336eb7d8-27df-584e-adc9-df5d1de8bc4e"] ["question-336eb7d8-27df-584e-adc9-df5d1de8bc4e" :question/math-academy-id "q-344058"] ["question-336eb7d8-27df-584e-adc9-df5d1de8bc4e" :question/problem "Select the missing parts in a particular solution of the differential equation ${y}^{′}-3y=f(x),$ where the Fourier series of the $6$-periodic forcing function is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼-3+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{6}{{n}^{2}\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}).\n$$\n\nThe Fourier series of a particular solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p}∼{{field-1}} & +{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,{{field-2}}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}) \\\\  & +{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,{{field-3}}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-336eb7d8-27df-584e-adc9-df5d1de8bc4e" :question/worked-solution "We assume that a solution of our equation has the following Fourier series:\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}).\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p}^{′} & ∼\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})) \\\\  & ∼0+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\cdot (-\\frac{n\\pi }{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}))+{b}_{n}\\cdot \\frac{n\\pi }{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}) \\\\  & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-\\frac{{a}_{n}n\\pi }{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})+\\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the expressions for ${y}_{p}^{′}$ and ${y}_{p}$ into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ({\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-\\frac{{a}_{n}n\\pi }{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})+\\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})) \\\\  & \\,-3(\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})) \\\\  & \\,\\,=-3+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{6}{{n}^{2}\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRearranging the terms, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & -3\\cdot \\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }(\\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{3}-3{a}_{n})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}) \\\\  & \\,\\,+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }(-\\frac{{a}_{n}n\\pi }{3}-3{b}_{n})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}) \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,=-3+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{6}{{n}^{2}\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, equating the free terms and the coefficients next to sines and cosines, we obtain the following system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-3\\cdot \\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}=-3 \\\\ \\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{3}-3{a}_{n}=\\frac{6}{{n}^{2}\\pi } \\\\ -\\frac{{a}_{n}n\\pi }{3}-3{b}_{n}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, ${a}_{0}=2,$ which means the constant term is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}=1.\n$$\n\nNext, from the third equation, \n\n$$\n{b}_{n}=-\\frac{{a}_{n}n\\pi }{9}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation gives\n\n$$\n(-\\frac{{a}_{n}n\\pi }{9})\\frac{n\\pi }{3}-3{a}_{n}=\\frac{6}{{n}^{2}\\pi }\\,⇒\\,{a}_{n}=-\\frac{162}{{n}^{2}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+81)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, for ${a}_{n}$ with $n\\ge 1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{n} & =-\\frac{{a}_{n}n\\pi }{9} \\\\  & =-\\frac{n\\pi }{9}\\cdot (-\\frac{162}{{n}^{2}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+81)}) \\\\  & =\\frac{18}{n({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+81)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p}∼1 & +{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,-\\frac{162}{{n}^{2}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+81)}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}) \\\\  & +{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,\\frac{18}{n({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+81)}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-336eb7d8-27df-584e-adc9-df5d1de8bc4e" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-319f9cc5-6350-50bc-9ef5-9fc966e9afe8" :answer-field/id #uuid "319f9cc5-6350-50bc-9ef5-9fc966e9afe8"] ["answer-b7737c7e-9824-5e5f-a3ae-34856a098e7c" :answer/id #uuid "b7737c7e-9824-5e5f-a3ae-34856a098e7c"] ["answer-b7737c7e-9824-5e5f-a3ae-34856a098e7c" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-b7737c7e-9824-5e5f-a3ae-34856a098e7c" :answer/value "-1"] ["answer-ab11db4e-65b6-5238-aa40-285ffcaa4e1d" :answer/id #uuid "ab11db4e-65b6-5238-aa40-285ffcaa4e1d"] ["answer-ab11db4e-65b6-5238-aa40-285ffcaa4e1d" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-ab11db4e-65b6-5238-aa40-285ffcaa4e1d" :answer/value "-2"] ["answer-efdbe697-d6a3-508c-a692-ae48f85ba690" :answer/id #uuid "efdbe697-d6a3-508c-a692-ae48f85ba690"] ["answer-efdbe697-d6a3-508c-a692-ae48f85ba690" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-efdbe697-d6a3-508c-a692-ae48f85ba690" :answer/value "1"] ["answer-55053340-f635-546e-8e5d-4621e256edb8" :answer/id #uuid "55053340-f635-546e-8e5d-4621e256edb8"] ["answer-55053340-f635-546e-8e5d-4621e256edb8" :answer/type