" :answer-field/choices "answer-1b3542e3-4bf3-5d25-87cb-feba5f3ffd90"] ["answer-field-44914850-8fa0-5396-b873-81fa2f52fbd0" :answer-field/choices "answer-5558f4a3-3994-5897-8ff9-622d5df04392"] ["question-336eb7d8-27df-584e-adc9-df5d1de8bc4e" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-319f9cc5-6350-50bc-9ef5-9fc966e9afe8"] ["question-336eb7d8-27df-584e-adc9-df5d1de8bc4e" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-cdd62ed7-f5a0-5d14-b295-af477d1b5a66"] ["question-336eb7d8-27df-584e-adc9-df5d1de8bc4e" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-44914850-8fa0-5396-b873-81fa2f52fbd0"] [17592186221455 :knowledge-point/questions "question-336eb7d8-27df-584e-adc9-df5d1de8bc4e"] [17592186222035 :question/problem "Select the missing parts in a particular solution of the differential equation ${y}^{″}-9y=f(x),$ where the Fourier series of the $2$-periodic forcing function is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{\\pi }{{n}^{3}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x).\n$$\n\n*Hint: You may assume that the free term and all the sine coefficients in the Fourier series of the particular solution are equal to zero.*\n\nThe Fourier series of a particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,{{field-1}}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x)\n$$"] [17592186222035 :question/worked-solution "We assume that a solution of our equation has the following Fourier series:\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x).\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p}^{′} & ∼\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x))∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-{a}_{n}n\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi x) \\\\ {y}_{p}^{″} & ∼\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-{a}_{n}n\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi x))∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-{a}_{n}{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the expressions for ${y}_{p}^{″}$ and ${y}_{p}$ into the equation and have\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-{a}_{n}{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x)-9({\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x))={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{\\pi }{{n}^{3}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x).\n$$\n\nRearranging the terms, we get \n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-{a}_{n}({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+9)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x)={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{\\pi }{{n}^{3}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x).\n$$\n\nNow, equating the cosine coefficients, we obtain \n\n$$\n-{a}_{n}({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+9)=\\frac{\\pi }{{n}^{3}}\\,⇒\\,{a}_{n}=-\\frac{\\pi }{{n}^{3}({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+9)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,-\\frac{\\pi }{{n}^{3}({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+9)}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x).\n$$"] [17592186222035 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-ec30d690-d89c-5e99-97e6-bdae59c5d3d2" :answer/id #uuid "ec30d690-d89c-5e99-97e6-bdae59c5d3d2"] ["answer-ec30d690-d89c-5e99-97e6-bdae59c5d3d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-ec30d690-d89c-5e99-97e6-bdae59c5d3d2" :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{n({n}^{3}\\pi -9)}"] ["answer-569abf23-828d-556a-8f5f-a80cd2b16ce5" :answer/id #uuid "569abf23-828d-556a-8f5f-a80cd2b16ce5"] ["answer-569abf23-828d-556a-8f5f-a80cd2b16ce5" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-569abf23-828d-556a-8f5f-a80cd2b16ce5" :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{{n}^{3}({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+9)}"] ["answer-ff05bb1d-0d47-5a0b-9d42-84f03013e335" :answer/id #uuid "ff05bb1d-0d47-5a0b-9d42-84f03013e335"] ["answer-ff05bb1d-0d47-5a0b-9d42-84f03013e335" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-ff05bb1d-0d47-5a0b-9d42-84f03013e335" :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{n}^{3}{\\pi }^{2}({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}-9)}"] ["answer-a4c02cbf-419a-5b32-acdf-ac8babf2fa7a" :answer/id #uuid "a4c02cbf-419a-5b32-acdf-ac8babf2fa7a"] ["answer-a4c02cbf-419a-5b32-acdf-ac8babf2fa7a" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-a4c02cbf-419a-5b32-acdf-ac8babf2fa7a" :answer/value "\\frac{n+1}{{n}^{3}{\\pi }^{2}+9}"] [17592186220900 :answer-field/correct "answer-569abf23-828d-556a-8f5f-a80cd2b16ce5"] [17592186220900 :answer-field/choices "answer-ec30d690-d89c-5e99-97e6-bdae59c5d3d2"] [17592186220900 :answer-field/choices "answer-569abf23-828d-556a-8f5f-a80cd2b16ce5"] [17592186220900 :answer-field/choices "answer-ff05bb1d-0d47-5a0b-9d42-84f03013e335"] [17592186220900 :answer-field/choices "answer-a4c02cbf-419a-5b32-acdf-ac8babf2fa7a"] ["question-f846bdbb-b4eb-53cc-9341-26d00f9d6239" :question/id #uuid "f846bdbb-b4eb-53cc-9341-26d00f9d6239"] ["question-f846bdbb-b4eb-53cc-9341-26d00f9d6239" :question/math-academy-id "q-343906"] ["question-f846bdbb-b4eb-53cc-9341-26d00f9d6239" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation ${y}^{″}+{\\pi }^{2}y=f(x),$ where the $2$-periodic forcing function is given by \n\n$$\nf(x)∼4+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{9}{{n}^{2}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi x).\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below regarding the resonant component of a particular solution of the equation.\n\nThe natural frequency of the system matches the frequency of the {{field-1}} harmonic of the forcing function. \n\nConsequently, the particular solution contains a resonant term of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{{p}_{1}}={{field-2}}.\n$$"] ["question-f846bdbb-b4eb-53cc-9341-26d00f9d6239" :question/worked-solution "We begin by identifying resonance. The differential equation \n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+{\\pi }^{2}y=f(x)\n$$\n\nhas a natural frequency of \n\n$$\n\\omega =\\sqrt{{\\pi }^{2}}=\\pi .\n$$\n\nThe frequencies of the forcing harmonics for a $2$-periodic function $(L=1)$ are \n\n$$\n{\\omega }_{n}=\\frac{n\\pi }{1}=n\\pi .\n$$\n\nFor $n=1$, we have ${\\omega }_{1}=\\pi .$ Since ${\\omega }_{1}=\\omega ,$ the $n=1$ harmonic of the forcing function causes resonance.\n\nFor the $n=1$ harmonic, the forcing term is \n\n$$\n{f}_{1}(x)=9\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x).\n$$\n\nBecause this frequency matches the natural frequency, we assume a particular solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{{p}_{1}}=x(A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)).\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{{p}_{1}}^{′} & =(A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x))+x(-\\pi A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)+\\pi B\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)) \\\\ {y}_{{p}_{1}}^{″} & =-2\\pi A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)+2\\pi B\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)-{\\pi }^{2}x(A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the expressions for ${y}_{{p}_{1}}^{″}$ and ${y}_{{p}_{1}}$ into the equation ${y}^{″}+{\\pi }^{2}y=9\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x):$\n\n$$\n[-2\\pi A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)+2\\pi B\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)-{\\pi }^{2}{y}_{{p}_{1}}]+{\\pi }^{2}{y}_{{p}_{1}}=9\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)\n$$\n\nThe resonant terms involving $x$ cancel out, leaving\n\n$$\n-2\\pi A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)+2\\pi B\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)=9\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x).\n$$\n\nNow, equating the sine and cosine coefficients, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-2\\pi A=9 \\\\ 2\\pi B=0\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}A=-\\frac{9}{2\\pi } \\\\ B=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the resonant component of a particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{{p}_{1}}=-\\frac{9x}{2\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x).\n$$"] ["question-f846bdbb-b4eb-53cc-9341-26d00f9d6239" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-8ce88b2e-b185-5d2e-8cfe-5be89cc0aa87" :answer-field/id #uuid "8ce88b2e-b185-5d2e-8cfe-5be89cc0aa87"] ["answer-ccea3e9e-29c1-513f-99b9-7b21823c4113" :answer/id #uuid "ccea3e9e-29c1-513f-99b9-7b21823c4113"] ["answer-ccea3e9e-29c1-513f-99b9-7b21823c4113" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-ccea3e9e-29c1-513f-99b9-7b21823c4113" :answer/value "n=1"] ["answer-27429d6e-d26b-57af-88d8-b3b645dceff5" :answer/id #uuid "27429d6e-d26b-57af-88d8-b3b645dceff5"] ["answer-27429d6e-d26b-57af-88d8-b3b645dceff5" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-274